<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Antibiotics Ultimate Mind Map & Clinical Scenarios</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: 'Helvetica Neue', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            color: #1e293b;
            background-color: #f8fafc;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .container {
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background: #ffffff;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.05);
        }

        .main-header {
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #002244, #004488);
            color: #ffffff;
            padding: 30px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 40px;
        }

        .main-header h1 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: 28px;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
        }

        .main-header p {
            margin: 10px 0 0 0;
            color: #93c5fd;
            font-size: 14px;
        }

        /* MIND MAP VISUAL GRID */
        .mindmap-grid {
            display: grid;
            grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
            gap: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 50px;
        }

        .map-card {
            border: 2px solid #e2e8f0;
            border-radius: 10px;
            padding: 20px;
            background: #ffffff;
            position: relative;
            transition: all 0.3s ease;
        }

        .map-card:hover {
            border-color: #004488;
            box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0,68,136,0.08);
        }

        .card-title {
            font-size: 16px;
            font-weight: 700;
            color: #004488;
            border-bottom: 2px solid #f1f5f9;
            padding-bottom: 8px;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            text-transform: uppercase;
        }

        .card-title::before {
            content: "➔ ";
            margin-right: 8px;
            color: #3b82f6;
        }

        .tree-node {
            margin-left: 15px;
            padding-left: 15px;
            border-left: 2px dashed #cbd5e1;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .node-title {
            font-weight: 600;
            font-size: 14px;
            color: #0f172a;
        }

        .node-details {
            font-size: 13px;
            color: #475569;
            margin-top: 2px;
        }

        .highlight-cidal { color: #dc2626; font-weight: bold; }
        .highlight-static { color: #d97706; font-weight: bold; }

        /* CLINICAL SCENARIOS SECTION */
        .scenario-section {
            background: #f1f5f9;
            padding: 25px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            border-top: 4px solid #004488;
            margin-top: 40px;
        }

        .scenario-box {
            background: #ffffff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
        }

        .scenario-tag {
            background: #004488;
            color: #ffffff;
            font-size: 11px;
            padding: 3px 8px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            font-weight: bold;
            display: inline-block;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        .scenario-text {
            font-size: 14px;
            font-weight: 600;
            color: #0f172a;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        .choice-container {
            display: flex;
            flex-direction: column;
            gap: 8px;
        }

        .choice-item {
            font-size: 13px;
            padding: 10px;
            background: #f8fafc;
            border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
            border-radius: 6px;
            cursor: pointer;
        }

        .choice-item.correct {
            background: #dcfce7;
            border-color: #22c55e;
            color: #14532d;
            font-weight: bold;
        }

        .rationale {
            margin-top: 8px;
            font-size: 12px;
            color: #64748b;
            font-style: italic;
            padding-left: 10px;
            border-left: 3px solid #22c55e;
        }

        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .mindmap-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="container">
        <!-- HEADER -->
        <div class="main-header">
            <h1>Introduction to Antibiotics Master Mind Map</h1>
            <p>Faculty of Medicine • Suez University • Visual Core Integration Map</p>
        </div>

        <!-- VISUAL MIND MAP MAP -->
        <div class="mindmap-grid">
            
            <!-- BLOCK 1: CORE CLASSIFICATION -->
            <div class="map-card">
                <div class="card-title">1. Core Class &amp; Kinetics Integration</div>
                
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Bactericidal Agents (Kill directly)[span_2](start_span)[span_2](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Target cell wall, cell membrane, or DNA replication processes[span_3](start_span)[span_3](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Bacteriostatic Agents (Halt growth)[span_4](start_span)[span_4](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Target protein synthesis (except aminoglycosides) or folate synthesis[span_5](start_span)[span_5](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Concentration-Dependent Killing[span_6](start_span)[span_6](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Higher peak above MIC = faster death. Features PAE[span_7](start_span)[span_7](end_span). <br><strong>Examples:</strong> Aminoglycosides, Quinolones[span_8](start_span)[span_8](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Time-Dependent Killing[span_9](start_span)[span_9](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Efficacy depends on time spent above MIC[span_10](start_span)[span_10](end_span). <br><strong>Examples:</strong> Beta-lactams, Macrolides, Clindamycin, Linezolid[span_11](start_span)[span_11](end_span).</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- BLOCK 2: TARGETS & MECHANISMS -->
            <div class="map-card">
                <div class="card-title">2. Structural Targets Mapping</div>
                
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Cell Wall Synthesis Inhibitors[span_12](start_span)[span_12](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Beta-lactams (Penicillins, Cephalosporins, Carbapenems, Monobactams), Vancomycin, Bacitracin[span_13](start_span)[span_13](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Protein Synthesis Inhibitors[span_14](start_span)[span_14](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ <strong>30S Subunit:</strong> Tetracyclines, Aminoglycosides[span_15](start_span)[span_15](end_span).<br>➔ <strong>50S Subunit:</strong> Macrolides, Clindamycin, Linezolid, Chloramphenicol, Streptogramins[span_16](start_span)[span_16](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Nucleic Acid &amp; Folate Paths[span_17](start_span)[span_17](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ <strong>DNA Gyrase:</strong> Quinolones | <strong>RNA Polymerase:</strong> Rifampin[span_18](start_span)[span_18](end_span).<br>➔ <strong>Folate Synthesis Blockers:</strong> Sulfonamides, Trimethoprim[span_19](start_span)[span_19](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Cell Membrane Disruptors[span_20](start_span)[span_20](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Polymyxins[span_21](start_span)[span_21](end_span).</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- BLOCK 3: RESISTANCE PATHWAYS -->
            <div class="map-card">
                <div class="card-title">3. Resistance Channels</div>
                
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Genetic Origin[span_22](start_span)[span_22](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ <strong>Chromosomal:</strong> Spontaneous random mutations[span_23](start_span)[span_23](end_span).<br>➔ <strong>Extrachromosomal (Plasmids):</strong> Horizontal gene transfer[span_24](start_span)[span_24](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Horizontal Transfer Mechanisms[span_25](start_span)[span_25](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ <strong>Conjugation:</strong> Sex pilus direct contact (Most Important)[span_26](start_span)[span_26](end_span).<br>➔ <strong>Transduction:</strong> Via Bacteriophage virus vector[span_27](start_span)[span_27](end_span).<br>➔ <strong>Transformation:</strong> Soluble naked DNA uptake from environment[span_28](start_span)[span_28](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title">Biochemical Mechanisms[span_29](start_span)[span_29](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ 1. Inactivating Enzymes | 2. Decreased accumulation (Efflux)[span_30](start_span)[span_30](end_span).<br>➔ 3. Target Site Modification | 4. Alternative metabolic pathway[span_31](start_span)[span_31](end_span).</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- BLOCK 4: PREGNANCY SAFETY INFOGRAPHIC -->
            <div class="map-card">
                <div class="card-title">4. FDA Pregnancy Safety Matching</div>
                
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title" style="color: #16a34a;">Category B (Safe to Use)[span_32](start_span)[span_32](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Beta-lactams, Cephalosporins, Macrolides (Erythromycin/Azithromycin), Clindamycin, Metronidazole[span_33](start_span)[span_33](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title" style="color: #ea580c;">Category C (Caution / Risk Unproven)[span_34](start_span)[span_34](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Fluoroquinolones, Chloramphenicol, Vancomycin, Clarithromycin, Trimethoprim[span_35](start_span)[span_35](end_span).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="tree-node">
                    <span class="node-title" style="color: #dc2626;">Category D (Proven Risk - Avoid if possible)[span_36](start_span)[span_36](end_span)</span>
                    <div class="node-details">➔ Tetracyclines (Tooth/Bone toxicity), Aminoglycosides (Ototoxicity)[span_37](start_span)[span_37](end_span).</div>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>

        <!-- CLINICAL SCENARIOS SECTION -->
        <div class="scenario-section">
            <h2>Interactive Clinical Scenarios (Active Recall)</h2>
            <p style="font-size: 13px; color: #475569; margin-top: -10px; margin-bottom: 20px;">Test your dynamic clinical reasoning based strictly on the lecture guidelines[span_38](start_span)[span_38](end_span):</p>

            <!-- Scenario 1 -->
            <div class="scenario-box">
                <div class="scenario-tag">Scenario 1: Pregnancy Safety[span_39](start_span)[span_39](end_span)</div>
                <div class="scenario-text">A 26-year-old pregnant woman in her second trimester presents with a severe respiratory infection. Which of the following options represents the safest choice of antibiotic for this patient?[span_40](start_span)[span_40](end_span)</div>
                <div class="choice-container">
                    <div class="choice-item">A) Doxycycline (A Tetracycline)</div>
                    <div class="choice-item correct">B) Ceftriaxone (A Cephalosporins agent - Category B)[span_41](start_span)[span_41](end_span)
                        <div class="rationale">Rationale: Cephalosporins and Beta-lactams are Category B, making them safe for use during pregnancy, whereas Tetracyclines are Category D due to skeletal risk[span_42](start_span)[span_42](end_span).</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="choice-item">C) Ciprofloxacin (A Fluoroquinolone)</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Scenario 2 -->
            <div class="scenario-box">
                <div class="scenario-tag">Scenario 2: Dosing Optimization &amp; Kinetics[span_43](start_span)[span_43](end_span)</div>
                <div class="scenario-text">You are adjusting the dose of Gentamicin (an Aminoglycoside) for a hospitalized patient. Based on its specific killing kinetics pattern, what is the best approach?[span_44](start_span)[span_44](end_span)</div>
                <div class="choice-container">
                    <div class="choice-item">A) Give continuous low-dose IV infusion to keep the concentration static right at the MIC boundary</div>
                    <div class="choice-item correct">B) Administer a high-dose once-daily bolus to maximize the peak concentration above the MIC[span_45](start_span)[span_45](end_span)
                        <div class="rationale">Rationale: Aminoglycosides exhibit concentration-dependent killing and a strong Postantibiotic Effect (PAE); high once-daily peaks optimize bacterial eradication[span_46](start_span)[span_46](end_span).</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="choice-item">C) Add a bacteriostatic drug like Erythromycin to stop replication while lowering the Gentamicin dosage</div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Scenario 3 -->
            <div class="scenario-box">
                <div class="scenario-tag">Scenario 3: Antibiotic Combinations Rule[span_47](start_span)[span_47](end_span)</div>
                <div class="scenario-text">A student proposes combining Penicillin G (a bactericidal cell wall inhibitor) with Tetracycline (a bacteriostatic 30S inhibitor) to treat a complex single-pathogen infection. Why is this combination clinically inappropriate?[span_48](start_span)[span_48](end_span)</div>
                <div class="choice-container">
                    <div class="choice-item">A) It represents a Synergistic relationship (1+1=3) which will cause sudden host cell lysis</div>
                    <div class="choice-item">B) Both drugs compete directly for the exact same active site on the 50S ribosome unit</div>
                    <div class="choice-item correct">C) It is fundamentally dynamic antagonism; bacteriostatic drugs arrest growth, which prevents bactericidal drugs (like Penicillin) from working effectively on actively dividing cell walls[span_49](start_span)[span_49](end_span)
                        <div class="rationale">Rationale: The lecture states you must never combine bactericidal and bacteriostatic agents against the same organism because cidal drugs require active bacterial replication to work[span_50](start_span)[span_50](end_span).</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>

</body>
</html>

